  "baseline_commit": "4b93b61",
  "scope": "Main shared C++/Python ImGui contrast panel exposes Keep current adjustment and parameter-free promote_rgb_contrast_stage. Copy/admit native session before replacing intent; freeze current mapping/components/selection, create identity draft with same components, retain stack policy and prior visits, clear transient Auto cycle and preview before recomputation. Busy/refused/scalar/uniform contexts are rejected. Reset retains saved stages; complete session Apply/recording and paired Undo/Redo are connected. Fifty-six independent literal-byte tests cover seven components, stack/selection choices and action/physical button; three refusal cases cover scalar, uniform and extra fields. A native C++ headless input test physically clicks the new button and verifies exact composed bytes, complete record and history. Windows/Linux each pass 20479 installed Python checks, six native groups, final extended contrast-panel group and three standalone UI probes. Initial new-test Undo checkpoint used a snapshot from before a later selection edit; corrected to the actual pre-Apply snapshot with unchanged implementation and pixel expectations; original failing report/source variant retained. Source inputs and retained product identities are checked before sealing; actual disposable venv interpreters import installed modules. Temporary assets are CRC/member-SHA archived before confined cleanup; qualified installs/native carriers/probes/logs remain. Existing historical Auto fingerprint failure and all99 triples remain unchanged. This closes explicit stage creation only, not full stage/visit editing or ImageJ/Fiji/platform/resource acceptance.",
